<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tata Steel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1907">1907</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tata Iron and Steel Company</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a>, founded in 1907 as the Tata Iron and Steel Company, is an Indian steel maker and one of the oldest industrial companies of the subcontinent. Planned by Jamsetji Tata and launched by his son Dorabji, it built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s first large integrated steel works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamshedpur">Jamshedpur</a>, which began production in 1912 using ore from Mayurbhanj. It is part of the Tata Group.</p></div>
